            "content": "Analyze the following thread to construct its Concurrency Contract.\nFork statement: pthread_create(&net_thread, NULL, net_event_thread_func, NULL)\nThread entry function body:\n```cpp\nvoid* net_event_thread_func(void* arg) {\n    // 1. First event arrives.\n    cma_netevent_callback(&g_cm_id, true);\n    printf(\"[NetEvent Thread] Queued first work item. Work data = 0x%lX.\\\\n\", g_cm_id.net_work.data);\n\n    // 2. Signal the worker thread that work is pending, but make it wait.\n    pthread_barrier_wait(&barrier_work_queued);\n\n    // 3. RACE WINDOW: A second event arrives *before* the first is processed.\n    printf(\"[NetEvent Thread] Second event arrived before first was processed.\\\\n\");\n    cma_netevent_callback(&g_cm_id, false);\n    printf(\"[NetEvent Thread] Corrupted pending work item. Work data = 0x%lX.\\\\n\", g_cm_id.net_work.data);\n\n\n    // 4. Signal the worker thread that it can now proceed with the corrupted work.\n    pthread_barrier_wait(&barrier_work_corrupted);\n    return NULL;\n}\n```",
            "role": "user"
        },
